# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
import editor/bim_editor.dl

function check modify input {boolean:passed} named {a string:caption}:
    execute:
        if passed = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + caption) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + caption) as a line

function type modify point text {a string:written} into {a pointer to a bim editor record:editor}:
    execute:
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of written:
            set code to (the character at cursor in written) as an integer
            type bim editor character code in editor

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
set lineId to add bim line on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.0 and y 0.0) to (the address of (editor's documentValue's current))
select bim editor bim sketch picked numbered lineId in e
type bim editor key 2002 in e
type modify point text (the string form of "#0,0") into e
type bim editor key bim enter key code in e
check modify input (editor's moveStage = 2) named (the string form of "absolute coordinate input sets the copy base")
type modify point text (the string form of "@3,4") into e
check modify input ((the cad distance from editor's snap's point to (a cad vector2 with x 3.0 and y 4.0)) < 1e-9) named (the string form of "relative coordinates update the indicated copy point while typing")
set previewChanges to the bim modify preview changes of editor
check modify input ((the length of previewChanges) = 1) named (the string form of "numeric copy input provides a ghost transform")
check modify input ((the length of (editor's documentValue's current's sketches's values)) = 1) named (the string form of "copy preview does not mutate the source model")
type bim editor key bim enter key code in e
set copied to the item at 1 in (editor's documentValue's current's sketches's values)
check modify input ((the cad distance from (the item at 0 in (copied's points's values)) to (a cad vector2 with x 3.0 and y 4.0)) < 1e-9) named (the string form of "Enter commits the exact typed copy displacement")
check modify input (editor's selectionId = copied's id) named (the string form of "new copies become selected")
check modify input (editor's moveStage = 1) named (the string form of "multiple copy asks for a new base point")
type bim editor key bim escape key code in e
check modify input (editor's tool = bim select tool) named (the string form of "Escape leaves copy without adding another element")

ignore undo bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
select bim editor bim sketch picked numbered lineId in e
type bim editor key 2002 in e
move bim editor pointer to (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) within 0.01 in e
press bim editor pointer in e
release bim editor pointer in e
move bim editor pointer to (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 0.0) within 0.01 in e
type modify point text (the string form of "2") into e
set validPoint to editor's snap's point
set beforeInvalidUndo to the length of (editor's documentValue's undoStack's values)
set beforeInvalidRedo to the length of (editor's documentValue's redoStack's values)
set beforeInvalidCount to the length of (editor's documentValue's current's sketches's values)
type modify point text (the string form of "/") into e
move bim editor pointer to (a cad vector2 with x 9.0 and y 0.0) within 0.01 in e
type bim editor key bim enter key code in e
check modify input ((editor's tool = bim copy tool) and (editor's moveStage = 2)) named (the string form of "incomplete point expression remains active after Enter")
check modify input ((the cad distance from editor's snap's point to validPoint) < 1e-9) named (the string form of "invalid typed point does not jump to the pointer")
check modify input ((the length of (editor's documentValue's current's sketches's values)) = beforeInvalidCount) named (the string form of "invalid point expression does not create geometry")
check modify input (((the length of (editor's documentValue's undoStack's values)) = beforeInvalidUndo) and ((the length of (editor's documentValue's redoStack's values)) = beforeInvalidRedo)) named (the string form of "invalid point expression preserves undo and redo")
type bim editor key bim escape key code in e
select bim editor bim sketch picked numbered lineId in e
type bim editor key 2016 in e
set editor's moveStage to 2
set editor's moveBase to a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0
type modify point text (the string form of "2/") into e
type bim editor key bim enter key code in e
check modify input ((editor's tool = bim scale tool) and ((the length of editor's numeric) = 2)) named (the string form of "incomplete scale expression remains editable after Enter")
set unchangedLine to the item at (the bim sketch index of lineId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's sketches's values)
check modify input (((the item at 1 in (unchangedLine's points's values))'s x) = 2.0) named (the string form of "invalid scale expression leaves source geometry unchanged")

type bim editor key bim escape key code in e
select bim editor bim sketch picked numbered lineId in e
type bim editor key 2016 in e
type bim editor key 258 in e
check modify input (editor's modify's copyMode and (editor's editMode = false)) named (the string form of "Tab toggles scale copy mode without entering geometry edit mode")
type bim editor key 2025 in e
type bim editor key 258 in e
check modify input (editor's modify's radial and (editor's editMode = false)) named (the string form of "Tab switches array layout without leaving the active tool")
